---
// Where the forward pass actually spends its time, from an ablation: strip the
// online-softmax work (the exp + running max/sum rescale) and re-time. At N=4096
// the kernel goes 52.0 ms → 51.0 ms — the softmax "glue" everyone teaches is
// ~2% of runtime. The other ~98% is the matmuls plus moving K/V and O through memory.
// Ablation (A100-80GB, B8 H16 d128 fp16): full 52.0 / no_exp 52.1 / no_softmax 51.0 ms.
const W = 640, H = 150;
const barX = 40, barY = 46, barW = 560, barH = 40;
const softmaxFrac = 0.02;                 // (52.0 - 51.0) / 52.0 ≈ 2%
const mmW = barW * (1 - softmaxFrac);
const smW = barW * softmaxFrac;
---
<figure class="chart">
  <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="A single horizontal bar showing where the forward pass spends its time. About 98% is matmul plus moving K, V, and the output through memory. About 2% is the online softmax — the exp and the running max and denominator rescaling. Removing the softmax work entirely takes the kernel from 52.0 to 51.0 milliseconds at N equals 4096, so the part of the algorithm everyone teaches is nearly free; the cost is the matmul and memory plumbing.">
    <text x={barX} y={30} class="ptitle">where the forward pass spends 52 ms (N=4096)</text>

    {/* matmul + memory plumbing */}
    <rect x={barX} y={barY} width={mmW} height={barH} rx="3" fill="var(--fg)" />
    <text x={barX + mmW / 2} y={barY + barH / 2 + 1} text-anchor="middle" class="seg-in">matmul + K/V/O memory plumbing</text>
    <text x={barX + mmW / 2} y={barY + barH / 2 + 15} text-anchor="middle" class="seg-in-sub">~98%</text>

    {/* online softmax */}
    <rect x={barX + mmW} y={barY} width={smW} height={barH} rx="3" fill="var(--accent)" />

    {/* callout line to the sliver */}
    <line x1={barX + mmW + smW / 2} y1={barY + barH} x2={barX + mmW + smW / 2} y2={barY + barH + 20} stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.2" />
    <text x={barX + barW} y={barY + barH + 33} text-anchor="end" class="acc-lbl">online softmax — the FlashAttention idea — ~2%</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>The forward pass, ablated: strip the online-softmax work (the <code>exp</code> and the running max/denominator rescale) and the kernel goes 52.0 → 51.0 ms at <code>N=4096</code>. The trick that <em>is</em> FlashAttention costs ~2% of runtime. The other ~98% is the two matmuls and streaming K/V and the output through memory — which is where the whole gap to SDPA lives.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .chart :global(.ptitle) { font-size: 13px; fill: var(--fg); font-family: var(--font-sans); font-weight: 600; }
  .chart :global(.seg-in) { font-size: 11.5px; fill: var(--bg); font-family: var(--font-sans); font-weight: 600; }
  .chart :global(.seg-in-sub) { font-size: 10px; fill: var(--bg); font-family: var(--font-mono); opacity: 0.85; }
  .chart :global(.acc-lbl) { font-size: 10.5px; fill: var(--accent); font-family: var(--font-mono); }
</style>
